Omnivox is a corporation of [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)|Syrin]], marked with a megaphone and known by the motto all of the media, all of the time. It makes and holds much of the media that airs across the planet and around [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)/Terminus|Terminus]], where it brings the convention [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)/Media Con|Media Con]]. Its chief executive is [[People/Braith Vanderbilt|Braith Vanderbilt]].

Its headquarters are the [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)/Golden Spire|Golden Spire]], a station in orbit over Syrin built out of a television station that had gone dark. Omnivox advertises the address openly: the station is best known for a casino that takes the very wealthy, and a stay there is a prize worth winning at the convention.

Omnivox holds the [[Org/Omnivox/Tarv of the Rising Moon|Tarv of the Rising Moon]] franchise. The character's first stories had him at war with the company, and after Omnivox bought them it had Tarv rewritten as one of its own heroes. Old readers keep to the earlier comics.
